  "_doc": "The chief of every Slagborn gang on the island, who went down the Throat to bargain with the fire itself and came back up part of it. P1 \"Chief's Due\": a great axe cone, a war-cry that calls a raider, and magma bursting out of four vents in the floor in turn. Two basalt dams (rocks) hold back the magma channel: break one and the flood runs past HIM (stun, takes more) — once each. P2 at 60% \"The Fire Answers\": he raises a ward of living fire; light the three Rim Shrine lamps the old pilgrims left down here to break it, while magma rings roll out from the vents. P3 new bar \"Heart of the Throat\": the Throat erupts — safe only next to a vent that has gone quiet (the vents), spreads on each player, a stack, and his axe now trails fire. OWNER #51 (2026-10-15): the phase that refilled the health bar is removed; the health bar is the whole fight.",
  "party": "Solo: very hard. 2-3: one lamp runner, a tank. 5: as designed.",
